the first three cars didn't
wanna give me a ride.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.100
I asked politely I wasn't intending

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.240
to rob them or any of that,

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.740
'cause that time being I
was kind of walling out,

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.290
robbing people for their phones and stuff

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.480
so I can sell it and get
money for crack or whatever.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.900
But at that time, I just really
simply just wanted a ride.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.080
He didn't say yes or no and
the third car that I hopped in,

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.490
he didn't say, so I stayed in
the car, he was on his phone.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.620
He picked up a client
and he's an Uber driver.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:19.010
And the next thing you know we're driving,

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:20.710
I'm thinking he's gonna give me a ride.

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:22.570
'Cause he didn't say yes
or no, he didn't respond.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.480
But actually in reality
he didn't speak English

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.220
and that's why he didn't spoke.

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:28.760
But I was led to believe
that, okay, I'ma get a ride,

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:31.080
but we're driving and he
got his client in the back

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.750
and we're driving in
the opposite direction.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.560
So I'm believing in my
heart he's not taking me

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.430
where I want to go.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:39.020
So I requested for him to stop the car

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:40.580
in the middle of the freeway,

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.990
because he's not going in
the direction I wanna go.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.970
And I grabbed the wheel.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:49.340
Boom, boom, boom, I
did a lotta bad things,

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.290
let's just put it like that.

00:11:50.290 --> 00:11:52.780
And it caused me to put my hands on him.

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:55.150
I didn't punch him or
anything in his face.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:56.152
I just shook him up.

00:11:56.152 --> 00:12:00.480
And doing things like that
is dangerous, it's violent.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:03.810
And then taking the phone,
that's, so it's robbery and fear

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:05.890
and being in San Mateo County,

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:06.840
they really don't play,

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:09.550
in San Francisco you can get
away with a lot of things.

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:14.550
So, I got in trouble and there you go.

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:17.370
So in a way getting in trouble

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:20.160
kinda got me to worry about
a lotta things I do now

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.820
'cause I can't afford
to get in any trouble.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.180
And a lotta things that I do do

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:25.680
nowadays is a lotta bad things.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.490
I shoplift, you know what I'm saying?

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.740
I do bad things and I'm
scared that I don't wanna go

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:33.850
to jail again, because any
felony can, if I get any felony,

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.010
I can go straight to
prison for like 32 months.

00:12:37.010 --> 00:12:39.680
I've never been in prison,
I've been in County jail.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.400
The most I ever did was six months.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.650
And when I did the six months,

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.360
I went to jail twice on my boyfriend.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.150
The second time he fell
in love with a woman

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.400
and it broke my heart and it sucks

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:51.517
'cause, you know, a
pretty girl, people like,

00:12:51.517 --> 00:12:52.780
"Why you don't have a boyfriend or a man?"

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:55.230
And I just don't, and
a lotta guys out here,

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.400
they don't take relationships serious.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:59.960
It's all about what you could do for them,

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.460
you would have to go to another country

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:06.290
and people value things over
there and value family, God,

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:09.880
and just all of that, over
here, nobody values nothing.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:11.910
Everybody takes everything for granted,

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.540
You know what I'm saying,
'cause we get everything handed

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.070
to us over here, it is true.

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:19.710
Like we get free phones, we get this,

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.130
it's just like, it's like that over here.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.780
And it sucks for the people that do work.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:25.190
They work hard for their money

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.050
and they don't get as much as we do.

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.050
And it's like a lotta
people look down on us

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:31.067
and I don't blame 'em, but yeah, so.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.180
- [Mark] How do you feel like,

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.293
this life, living on the
streets has changed you?

00:13:35.293 --> 00:13:37.503
Did you become more suspicious or?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.080
- It made me lower myself a lot.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.990
like I should believe I'm worth more

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:47.830
but I've like, I feel like, wow,

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:50.300
what I've like done
things for certain money

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.420
for the price just dropped tremendously.

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:56.330
And it's like sucks because like, wow,

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.163
you know what I'm saying?

00:13:57.163 --> 00:13:59.980
Like, I can't believe myself
for the drugs, and you know,

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:01.900
I dropped myself so low.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.190
And so, and it's just not
good to live like this,

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.300
not knowing where you're gonna sleep.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:10.340
So every day, like my hustle
and my thing is make money,

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:11.173
get a hotel.

00:14:11.173 --> 00:14:13.210
I learned to not put
the drugs first anymore.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.550
The drugs don't come first no more.

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:18.020
My hotel room comes first
'cause I need a place to stay

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:20.350
to do the drugs so I need a place.

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:22.660
So every day in the hotel I'm at,

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.990
they work with me like I can
pay some later, some now,

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.080
and I like that and they
let me bring a client

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.360
or two up there 'cause I spoke with them,

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.330
in order to pay that
rent I need their help

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.530
to, you know what I'm saying?

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:36.110
In order, I need to bring a
person to and they let me.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.543
So my room is first, then the drugs.

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.700
So that's how it goes.

00:14:42.248 --> 00:14:43.210
- [Mark] All right, Francesca,

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:44.089
